---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Header from '../components/Header.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
import Figure from '../components/Figure.astro';
import Fig5SystemsMap from '../components/Fig5SystemsMap.astro';
import IntakeForm from '../components/IntakeForm.astro';
---

<Base
  title="Start a systems map · Thread, Honolulu"
  description="A free systems map for one workflow in your business: what happens today, where the time goes, and a ranked list of what’s worth fixing first. Two a month."
>
  <Header />

  <section class="intake">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="doc">
        <div>
          <div class="eyebrow">Systems map · free · two a month</div>
          <h1>Start a systems map.</h1>
          <p class="lead" style="max-width:56ch">
            Fill this in and Thread draws how one workflow really moves through your
            business: every tool it touches, every handoff, and every point where a person
            is doing a job a system should be doing.
          </p>

          <p class="txt" style="margin-bottom:16px;max-width:56ch">
            <strong>This form is the first half of it.</strong> The more you put here, the
            less of the ninety minutes gets spent on questions you have already answered.
            Rough is fine. Nothing here needs to be exact.
          </p>
          <p class="txt" style="margin-bottom:16px;max-width:56ch">
            <strong>Then one conversation.</strong> Ninety minutes, with whoever actually
            does the work rather than only whoever owns it. That is the part that makes the
            map true.
          </p>
          <p class="txt" style="max-width:56ch">
            <strong>Then the map, within five business days.</strong> Yours to keep. If the
            honest answer is that you don’t need custom software, it will say so.
          </p>
        </div>

        <aside class="side">
          <span class="lbl">Before you start</span>
          Pick the one process that costs you the most time, and pick it before you fill
          this in. A map covers one workflow, not a whole business, which is what keeps it
          free and keeps it useful. Mapping everything is a paid engagement, and this is a
          reasonable way to find out whether that’s worth doing.
        </aside>
      </div>

      <IntakeForm kind="map" />
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="specimen-band">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="eyebrow">What you get back</div>
      <h2 style="margin:16px 0 22px;max-width:18ch">This, drawn from your business.</h2>
      <p class="lead" style="max-width:56ch">
        A specimen sheet, so you know what you’re asking for. Yours arrives with your
        stages, your tools and your frictions in it.
      </p>

      <Figure caption="Fig. 5 · Systems map, specimen sheet">
        <Fig5SystemsMap />
      </Figure>
    </div>
  </section>

  <Footer />
</Base>

<style>
  .intake { padding: 96px 0 0; }
  .intake h1 {
    font-size: clamp(34px, 4.4vw, 52px);
    margin: 20px 0 22px;
    max-width: 14ch;
  }
  /* The form sits below the document grid rather than in the margin column:
     ten fields would make that column a very long, very narrow ribbon. */
  .intake :global(.form) { margin-top: 44px; }
  .specimen-band { padding: 96px 0; }

  @media (max-width: 640px) {
    .intake { padding: 66px 0 0; }
    .specimen-band { padding: 66px 0; }
  }
</style>
